.TH diffh 1 "FUZIX System Utilities" "FUZIX"
.SH NAME
diffh \- compare two large files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B diffh
.I "file1 file2"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B diffh
reports the differences between two files in the same form as
.BR diff (1),
but works a window at a time rather than holding both files in memory.
.PP
It is what
.B diff
falls back on for files too big to do properly, and the price is that it
can miss a match that
.B diff
would have found: the answer is correct but not always the shortest one.
.SH NOTES
Use
.BR diff (1)
unless it runs out of memory.  On a machine this size, that happens
sooner than you would like.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR diff (1),
.BR cmp (1),
.BR comm (1)
